Z||000000||Cheever3000||12-10-2001||10:10 PM||||I've seen a few people here who are also active on the Fiero List email thing, but it seems they are mostly two different groups of people.  Does it seem that way to you?  Most of the Fiero owners in my town that I talk to are not on the Forum, but they are on the List.  Do you agree with me that the two are complimentary?  There are also the Yahoo-type groups and clubs, but I can see more of a difference with them.  Is the Forum more for visually-oriented people, and the List more for audio-orented?  <P>There's no problem here, and if there is a history of conflict between the two then I am not aware of it.  I just think it's a curiosity.  They each serve a need, and do it well IMO.  Am I mistaken, and there are really more people on both, than I realize?<P>What's your experience and observation regarding this?<BR><P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Cheever_gold_sig.jpg"> <BR><I>Try to keep up!</I>||||reg||5
Z||000001||My7Fieros||12-11-2001||03:16 AM||||I belonged to the Fiero mailing list a couple of years ago, before I joined Pennocks. I got out of it quick for a couple of reasons....first, its a diff setup than this one...its strictly a mailing list and your mail box gets flooded badly w/the emails (I mean like 30 or 40 a day)..I just didnt like the way it was set up.<BR>Second, the people on that list, at least at that time, were the absolute rudest people Ive ever encountered (e-encountered  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"> ). It may not be that way now, but man, talk about harsh! I have to admit though, w/all the silliness thats been going on here (no names mentioned Ed or rayb), this forum just isnt what it used to be.....oh well.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif">||||reg||1
